course: dictionary
lesson: 4382
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show which one is meant. «Ella's account had been hacked, and the hacker was asking everyone on her list.» Account and hacker are about computers, so hack here means to get into an account without permission.
explain: The same word can mean something very different in another sentence. Hack can also mean to cut roughly with hard, quick strokes, like with an axe. Explorers hack their way through a jungle: the clue is jungle, which has plants to cut through, not computers.
explain: In everyday talk, a «life hack» is a clever, quick trick that makes something easier, and a «hacking cough» is a rough, dry cough that keeps repeating. Always ask which meaning fits the clues around the word.
fact: Hack is a verb and a noun: you can hack at a branch, or you can use a hack, which is a trick.
fact: «Hack into» means to get into a computer or account without permission, often to steal or change information.
fact: «Hack through» and «hack away at» mean to cut roughly with hard, quick strokes.
fact: A «life hack» is a clever, quick trick that makes something easier.
fact: Strong passwords and two-step checks help stop people hacking into accounts.
exercise: «Ella's account had been hacked.» What does hacked mean here? | Cured of a cough | Made into a clever trick | *Got into it without permission | Cut down with an axe
exercise: «The explorers had to hack through the thick jungle.» What does hack through mean? | Fall asleep under a tree | Sing loudly as they walked | *Cut a path with hard, quick strokes | Get into a computer
exercise: «She had a hacking cough all week.» What does hacking describe? | A cut in the wood | A loud laugh | A clever trick for life | *A rough, dry, repeated cough
test: What is a life hack? | A rough, dry cough | *A clever, quick trick that makes life easier | A tent for camping | A fake computer account
test: «Strong passwords help stop anyone hacking into your account.» What does hacking into mean? | Cutting it roughly with an axe | Printing the account details | *Getting into it without permission | Thinking hard about the account
exam: Sam says, «I can't hack this homework, it is far too hard.» What does can't hack it mean? | Can't stop coughing | Can't find the password | *Can't cope with it | Can't cut it with a knife
